# STE-31 — copy to `be/.env.production` on the VPS and fill in.
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in copy. `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored except
# these examples; `PII_KEYS` opens every identity document Sterun holds and
# `SUSD_DISTRIBUTOR_SECRET` can move the entire test supply.
#
# Custody, rotation, and what to do if one of these leaks: be/OPERATIONS.md.

# --- the deployment ---------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=production
# The domain Caddy will get a certificate for. DNS must already point here.
STERUN_DOMAIN=api.sterun.example
# Origin allowed to call the API from a browser (the web app, STE-32).
# Deliberately not "*": authenticated requests carry a wallet signature.
STERUN_WEB_ORIGIN=https://sterun.example

# --- Postgres ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by compose.prod.yml to build DATABASE_URL. Generate, do not invent:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_USER=sterun
# POSTGRES_DB=sterun

# --- PII encryption (REQUIRED for the vault) --------------------------------
# The service refuses to start with a database and no key rather than storing
# identity documents in the clear.
#   node -e "console.log('1:'+require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
PII_KEYS=
PII_ACTIVE_KEY_ID=1

# --- network ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Contract addresses default to what docs/deployments.md records, which is
# baked into the image. Set these only to point somewhere else.
# STELLAR_NETWORK=testnet
# STELLAR_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# EVENT_REGISTRY=
# RACE_RECORD=
# SUSD_SAC=

# --- TTL keeper -------------------------------------------------------------
# Pays for ExtendFootprintTTLOp. Needs XLM and nothing else: extending a TTL
# requires no authorization, so this key controls no records and can spend
# nothing but its own fees. Without it the keeper container scans and reports
# but cannot submit, which is a slow leak rather than an outage — a record whose
# rent lapses is archived and breaks `verify` until it is restored.
TTL_KEEPER_SECRET=

# --- faucet (optional) ------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if this box hands out test sUSD. The API never uses it. Leaving
# it unset is the safer default for a public host.
# SUSD_DISTRIBUTOR_SECRET=

# --- logging ----------------------------------------------------------------
# LOG_LEVEL=info
